                                "sense_id": "6d082898-6552-37a6-a618-35cd3f359db2",
                                "text": "When the poplar leaves atremble\nTurn their edges to the light,"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "19f21183-913e-4252-8b61-b87737ea37ff",
                                "sense_id": "6d082898-6552-37a6-a618-35cd3f359db2",
                                "text": "To Jurgis this man’s whole presence reeked of the crime he had committed; the touch of his body […] set every nerve of him a-tremble […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "844fc244-8d59-4472-8186-62eb4245c410",
                                "sense_id": "6d082898-6552-37a6-a618-35cd3f359db2",
                                "text": "[…] he beheld a tear a-tremble on her eyelid."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b09edabf-d637-4c3e-a46d-45febc27d54b",
                                "sense_id": "6d082898-6552-37a6-a618-35cd3f359db2",
                                "text": "When her stomach felt better (but her legs were all atremble again, something lost, something gained), she looked at herself in the bathroom mirror."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
